## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design an online, latency-constrained text classifier with limited features and simple drift checks, testing hashing-based features, SGD/partial_fit, and streaming evaluation.

## Key Concepts
- Hashing-based text features (30 features)
- Online learning with partial_fit
- Latency constraints on CPU
- Drift checks and calibration
- Evaluation metrics for spam detection (precision, recall, F1, PR-AUC)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple online logistic regression with partial_fit (conceptual)
class OnlineLR {
  constructor(nFeatures){ this.w = new Float64Array(nFeatures); this.b = 0; }
  predict(x){ let s=this.b; for(let i=0;i<x.length;i++) s+= this.w[i]*x[i]; return 1/(1+Math.exp(-s)); }
  partial_fit(x,y,lr=0.1){ const p=this.predict(x); const g=y-p; for(let i=0;i<x.length;i++) this.w[i]+=lr*g*x[i]; this.b+=lr*g; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for multiclass spam types (phishing, promo, etc.)?
- What changes if label latency increases from seconds to minutes?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests on-device ML design under strict latency, privacy, and fairness constraints; requires end-to-end thinking from data flow to deployment.

## Key Concepts
- Edge ML and latency budgets
- Federated learning with DP
- Model compression (quantization/pruning)
- Fairness-aware ranking
- Rollback and drift monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Latency check scaffold (pseudo)
function measureLatency(model, input){
  const t0 = performance.now();
  model.infer(input);
  const t1 = performance.now();
  return t1 - t0;
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit fairness across departments while maintaining DP guarantees?
- What metrics and rollback triggers would you define for drift detection?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical NLP pipeline setup, handling class imbalance, and real-world deployment concerns for a beginner-friendly problem.

## Key Concepts
- TF-IDF vectorization with unigrams/bigrams
- Handling imbalanced data via class_weight
- Time-based train/test splits to mimic streaming data
- Evaluation: macro F1 and PR-AUC for imbalanced tasks
- Canary rollout and monitoring basics for production safety

## Code Example
